Happy Monday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Place stop loss order UAL September 18th $130 calls at $6.10, GTC

 

The S&P 500 is sharply higher as President Trump listens to the bond market.
 
The president claims talks are back on with Iran to end the war.
 
Energy prices are plummeting, and Treasury yields are falling, too.
 
These announcements from the president are predictable because he cannot win a war with the bond market.
 
If fixed-income traders slow the pace of Treasury buying, yields spike and things begin to break.
 
Airlines are the natural beneficiaries of these peace announcements because fuel is the largest cost for transportation companies.
 
UAL, DAL, and AAL are all screaming higher.
 
We added UAL calls late Friday.
 
We sold half this morning for a 62% gain!
 
We are placing a new stop-loss order on the remaining position, although we still hope to exit closer to $135.
 
These stop-loss orders are part of our new trade management strategy.
 
Letting winning trades become losers, like our DELL position, simply should not happen.
 
While stocks are higher today, it is important to remember that President Trump saying talks with Iran have resumed does not necessarily make it so.
 
Iran could deny any diplomatic progress.
 
It could also continue striking U.S. military assets.
 
Iran benefits from higher energy prices during negotiations, so a prolonged conflict gives it additional leverage.
 
Caution is still warranted.
 
We have been down this road before, where the president's words and reality did not align.
 
We really like the way TMDX is behaving, but earnings are due this week. We have shares headed to $94. We are passing.
 
MDB tested the breakout level this morning at $355. Be patient.
 
DELL is little changed.
 
Again, we are being patient because shares still appear to be on the verge of a significant breakout.
 
We are also watching the action in semiconductors and memory stocks.
 
They started weaker but quickly found a bid.
 
It is still too early to add puts or calls.
 
We continue to favor TER and will watch the group through Wednesday.
 
New Orders
➤ Place stop loss order UAL September 18th $130 calls at $6.10, GTC

 

