Happy Friday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy UAL September 18th $130 calls at $5.10,

 

The choppy trade continues this morning as a huge opening rally for the S&P 500 completely reverses. The benchmark opened above key resistance at 7,470, then promptly gave back all of the gains.The catalyst for the selling is energy prices. Brent Crude oil is up 1.5% to $88.26 per barrel. Bond yields are surging, with the 10-year above 4.7%. This is incredibly bearish for stocks and risk assets.Bond traders are telling President Trump to end the war or they will create a credit crisis. If he listens stocks will promptly march to new highs. If not, they will ruin his presidency.For those not paying attention, the story this week is about credit worries related to AI spending. This is nonsense. The problems in credit are related to energy prices. Shares of the biggest AI spenders are being accumulated.MSFT is up 18.7% this week. GOOGL is up 8%. AMZN is now up 16%, thanks to a 14% rally today.We closed our position in the AMZN August 21 $275 calls for $6.50.We like the way DELL and MDB are behaving. They are each now likely to finish this week above important resistance. We will hold.C and STZ are hanging-in. They are OK, but we want to see more downside progress sooner-than-later.We like RDDT short, to trade back to $120.We favor STX and UAL as longs. We have upside targets at $1,100, and $137, respectively.We are adding UAL calls because we believe President Trump will listen to bond traders.
 
