Happy Tuesday,
 
TLDR: No New Trades

 

The S&P 500 is modestly lower, but that does not begin to tell the story of the carnage in technology.
 
Specifically, semiconductors are getting walloped on worries about the AI buildout.
 
To make matters worse for tech investors, KO reported blowout earnings this morning, sending consumer staples stocks sharply higher.
 
Investors can contrast the safety of investing in a soda business versus semiconductors.
 
At least for today, the choice is easy.
 
The NDX is in a sticky spot because big tech needs to reverse immediately.
 
Key support was 28,000. A decisive move below that level will likely invite even more selling from professional money managers.
 
It is Tuesday, and turnarounds often happen on this day of the week.
 
But bulls are in a tough spot here.
 
Almost every other part of the market is behaving better than technology.
 
Financials and Materials are making new highs.
 
Insurance stocks are roaring higher as investors seek safety.
 
Speaking of which, VOE and QVAL are also making new highs.
 
Look at SNA and SWK.
 
We have upside targets of $435 and $102, respectively.
 
In short, professionals are not fleeing stocks. They are liquidating technology winners.
 
We know this because 2026 tech laggards are screaming higher.
 
We wrote yesterday about WDAY, SAP, and ADBE.
 
Add NOW to that mix of 2026 laggards that have finally found bids.
 
On the flip side, technology winners are getting hit hard.
 
DELL was holding up like a champ until Friday, when shares began to slip.
 
We need a close today above $388, which is still doable, but we will probably have to close the position later this week for a loss.
 
We closed MO for a small profit.
 
MO is bouncing with the flight to safety. The KO earnings are helping.
 
STZ is in that same boat.
 
This is a weak story that is getting a lift from the stronger consumer staples group.
 
We do not expect that to last, especially if technology rebounds.
 
We are holding.
 
We love the look of VRTX, but earnings are due on August 3.
 
We are passing.
 
BE truly looks like a short, but this still feels like playing with fire.
 
Shares could easily close back above $177 today, setting up a reversal on the daily chart.
 
No new trades today.

 

