TLDR: No New Trades

 

The S&P 500 popped on the open following news that the United States and Iran have suspended military strikes after two weeks of fighting.
 
Oil prices are careening lower.
 
West Texas Intermediate crude oil is trading at $83.65, down 6.8%. Brent crude is at $90.20, down 8.1%.
 
The yield on the 10-year Treasury note is 4.66%, down a fraction.
 
We are finally getting the action bulls needed a month ago for an orderly pullback.
 
Semiconductors are working lower as software stocks rally.
 
