AAOI has support at $88.50, its 200-day moving average. Shares are at $93, down 7.2%.
 
This might feel like the end of the world for semiconductors, but it is probably nothing more than a correction.
 
The QQQ has a gap at $682, the May 5 high.
 
It will be interesting to see if the widely held ETF magically finds a bid there.
 
We would be extremely careful pressing the short side of big tech down here.
 
Meanwhile, technology laggards, especially software, are screaming higher.
 
WDAY is up 8.5%, SAP is higher by 7%, and ADBE is gaining 5.4%.
 
The tape is volatile today, but the reversal from the early highs does not necessarily mean bears are back in control.
 
We are watching closely to see what happens as the QQQ and NDX fill their May 5 gaps.
 
We expect short covering to emerge later today.
 
No new trades.

 

