Happy Thursday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Sell half of STZ September 18th $130 puts at $8.75, GTC 

 

The S&P 500 opened today below its 20-day and 50-day moving averages near 7,470.
 
That is significant because technical traders are now in liquidation mode.
 
Iran-backed militants attacked two Saudi tankers.
 
West Texas Intermediate crude oil is trading at $91.59 per barrel, up 5.7%. International Brent crude is at $100.26 per barrel, up 6.8%.
 
The yield on the 10-year Treasury note is 4.7%, the highest level since the war with Iran began.
 
All of these numbers are bad, and they are trending in the wrong direction for bulls.
 
The lone piece of good news is technology earnings.
 
GOOGL reported great numbers, but the company is accelerating AI infrastructure spending, so traders are penalizing the stock.
 
AMZN is getting crushed in sympathy with GOOGL.
 
Traders believe AMZN will raise capex spending. Shares are now testing key support at $232. We expect a bounce from this level.
 
AMZN reports in one week.
 
The other side of rising AI infrastructure spending is more demand for infrastructure providers.
 
That is why MU, DELL, PWR, and VRT continue to show strength.
 
There is also strength in HUT.
 
We continue to believe shares can reach $140, assuming the broader market does not fall apart.
 
Bulls are in a tough spot because they need President Trump to indicate there is still a diplomatic solution to end the war with Iran.
 
He does not seem inclined to do that at the moment, but he is mercurial. Stay tuned.
 
We added STZ puts on Wednesday.
 
The position is behaving well. We continue to see a decline to at least $125 as traders retest the November 2025 lows.
 
We are placing a new order to sell half on that decline.
 
DELL is trending higher, but we are still looking to exit into a rally toward $460.
 
