Oil prices are surging after U.S. Secretary of State Rubio said any new Iran deal must guarantee free passage through the Strait of Hormuz.
 
That significantly changes the previous framework.
 
We do not want to sound conspiratorial, but it feels like the White House is trying to pressure stocks lower.
 
Oddly enough, traders are taking the other side by adding risk. It seems counterintuitive, but that is what the tape is showing.
 
The negative headlines keep coming as the S&P approaches new highs.
 
From renewed concerns over Iran to the promise of additional tariffs, there is no shortage of reasons for bears to lean in.
 
