Happy Thursday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy DELL August 21st $620 calls at $9.50, day order only

 

President Trump claimed today that Iran called after U.S. Central Command bombarded several targets earlier in the week.
 
Magically, oil prices are down and stock prices are up.
 
The manipulation of the stock market continues.
 
Semiconductors are front and center today.
 
They are roaring back after plummeting earlier in the week. AMAT, KLAC, and LRCX all tested their respective 50-day moving averages and bounced sharply.
 
That being said, for bulls to make real progress in the days and weeks ahead, semiconductors need to consolidate and digest gains.
 
That means more sideways action or further weakness, not another sprint to new highs.
 
Lagging technology groups like enterprise software need to begin participating.
 
We continue to favor DDOG, SNOW, and MDB in software.
 
MDB, in particular, is behaving well. We continue to see a rally to at least $400.
 
We closed our DELL position yesterday.
 
