Happy Wednesday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy half position HOOD August 21st $120 calls at $6.00 day order only 

 

Traders are starting the new quarter by selling winners and buying losers.
 
This is normal.
 
Professionals window dress their portfolios with the best-performing stocks during the quarter, right before the end of the reporting period.
 
What is happening now is the liquidation of those pretend positions.
 
That does not mean those stocks are destined to underperform in the second half. It is simply part of the normal ebb and flow of money managers wanting to look smarter than they really are.
 
We are seeing rotation into the losers, a.k.a. software.
 
There was a big upgrade this morning from Guggenheim on NOW, CRM, and CHKP. The selling in software platforms this year has been extreme.
 
Bears are covering short positions.
 
Our strategy is to find the charts with the best relative strength and buy those.
 
We got the right names. The execution, not so much.
 
We wrote last week about SNOW, DDOG, and CRWD reaching targets of $280, $280, and $775, respectively.
 
CRWD reached our target. SNOW and DDOG are getting close.
 
We wrote down HOOD for today.
 
We see shares climbing back to $112, then $119, as traders embrace the company's tokenization plans.
 
That said, we are buying only half of our normal position because there might be one more pullback to $96 to test the 20-day moving average.
 
MDB and TSLA are acting well.
 
MO is back at the 20-day moving average. It seems fine.
 
We had some questions about TSLA and time decay.
 
The reason we are not selling, even with the July 4th holiday approaching, is that we believe shares will respond positively to the upcoming end-of-quarter EV sales report. We expect that report around July 3.
 
