Happy Monday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy SNOW August 21st $300 Calls at $6.20 or Less

 

Better late than never.
 
We are finally getting the tape action bulls needed two weeks ago, when we wrote that a modest decline in semiconductors coupled with a rally in software stocks would sustain the bullish advance.
 
Software is surging. Semis are faltering.
 
That is not terrible. In fact, a consolidation of the massive first-half gains in semiconductors would be healthy.
 
The problem is software collapsed two weeks ago before it had a chance to take the baton.
 
We know this because we added MDB with the expectation that software would help sustain the technology bull market.
 
We are frustrated that the bulk of software's new strength arrived late Friday and again this morning before the opening bell.
 
We wrote about DDOG, SNOW, and CRWD with initial targets at $280, $280, and $775, respectively.
 
All three remain "buys".
 
That said, CRWD is already trading at $752 after a 7% move higher. Sheesh. Don't chase these.
 
MDB is trading at $332 and looks great, assuming the gains hold. The stock has the potential to run to $405, but bulls need to finish the job with a strong close.
 
TSLA is rallying ahead of quarter-end EV delivery numbers.
 
We continue to believe TSLA is primarily an EV and robotaxi story in the near term. It remains a good story, and the stock is beginning to act better.
 
MO is floating near unchanged.
 
That is perfectly fine. The stock serves as a useful hedge against a prolonged market decline, and we continue to expect shares to stretch toward $77. We are holding.
 
New Orders
➤ Buy SNOW August 21st $300 Calls at $6.20 or Less Day order only.

 

