Happy Friday,
 
TLDR: No New Trades 

 

The S&P 500 opened below its 50-day moving average at 7,356 and suddenly all news is bad news.
 
On Bloomberg today, economists are saying the decline in energy prices will actually cause inflation to accelerate because consumers will use their savings at the gas pump to snap up more products.
 
Forget that this is exactly the opposite of the narrative that has been in place since the Iran war.
 
The point is that when stocks are declining, economists and strategists rationalize. It rarely makes much sense. And that's fine.
 
The good news is that professionals appeared willing to buy the early decline today.
 
The bad news is that Friday afternoons can become excruciatingly long. We are not sure traders want to be long heading into the weekend.
 
The morning gains should fade a bit.
 
The technical picture is straightforward. A break below 7,356 brings the June 7 low into play. That level sits at 7,238. The early low this morning was 7,294.
 
The bottom line is that we should not get too excited about this bounce from the lows.
 
We have a number of stocks on both our buy and sell lists.
 
On the buy side, we really like the way DDOG, SNOW, and CRWD are behaving. When technology finds a short-term bottom, these stocks should rally toward $280, $280, and $775, respectively.
 
And yes, we will be call buyers.
 
On the short side, CSCO and ADI appear ready to make significant corrections. We have CSCO working back toward $108. ADI should decline to $382 initially, and then perhaps $363.
 
We would really like to buy ADI puts here. The problem is that we cannot find an August contract with enough open interest to make the trade worthwhile. So, we are passing.
 
MRNA is making a new high. We missed that one. That's completely on us. The pullback to the breakout level near $59 was perfect.
 
MDB and TSLA are better, but still not great. We are holding both as they set up again.
 
We added MO on Thursday.
 
The stock traded near $74 early this morning and should be able to stretch toward $77 within a week or so.
 
Nothing new for today.
 
The market is correcting through time more than price. That's constructive. We are seeing more stocks setting up than breaking down, and that usually leads to opportunity.
 
Be patient. We expect a much better hunting environment next week.
 
Sharpen your spears.

 

