TLDR: No New Trades

 

Stocks are rebounding this morning as bulls breathe a sigh of relief that Friday's weakness is not being met with immediate follow-through selling.
 
Ideally, we would have preferred a selling climax at the open. That type of washout tends to clear out weak hands and create a stronger foundation for a rally.
 
The problem for bulls remains interest rates.
 
The stronger-than-expected employment report has reinforced the narrative of a resilient economy and persistent inflation.
 
As long as that narrative remains intact, bond traders will continue demanding higher yields unless there is a compelling reason to believe inflation pressures are easing. Right now, energy prices remain ground zero in that debate.
 
From a tactical perspective, traders are testing resistance on the S&P 500 near 7,450. Bulls need a decisive close above that level sooner rather than later. Without that breakout, the path of least resistance likely becomes a drift lower toward the rising 50-day moving average near 7,175.
 
That type of pullback would not damage the broader bull market. It would, however, create considerable pain for momentum traders who have become accustomed to buying every dip.
 
We found only one compelling setup this morning. SPOT is breaking out of a small bullish flag and has a clear path toward $544. We like the pattern, but we are passing on the trade for now.
 
HOOD breaks out above $87. We believe that is entirely achievable and are willing to give the stock another day or two to make the move. The chart remains constructive.
 
TSLA fell through support at $414.50 on Friday and immediately accelerated lower. Some of that weakness appears tied to concerns surrounding a potential SpaceX IPO.
 
We believe the market is missing the bigger picture. TSLA remains the more compelling short-term story. We expect shares to reclaim the $414.50 level by Tuesday.
 
MRNA is our newest position. The stock has done little since entry, but we are not concerned.
 
The setup remains intact, and we expect momentum to improve as the week progresses.

 

