Happy Friday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy MRNA & Sell META

 

The latest Nonfarm payroll data hit the tape this morning and the numbers were much better than expected. The economy created 172,000 jobs last month, far above the 85,000 forecasts.
 
Ironically, this is bad news for stocks.
 
The payroll report reinforces the narrative of a strong economy and higher inflation. The natural progression of this storyline is the need for higher interest rates. While we expect Fed Chairman Warsh to resist rate hikes, he is ultimately at the mercy of fixed-income traders.
 
Bond traders will demand higher coupons unless there is some relief on inflation. This means the war with Iran, and the resulting rise in energy prices, must end.
 
President Trump can't win a war with bond traders. Nobody can. Hopefully Washington understands this.
 
The selling in technology shares is expected. That said, bulls need enterprise software stocks to hold in here. That leadership is important as semiconductors digest their gains.
 
We wrote recently that software needed to pick up the baton, and so far that is happening.
 
Some semis look extremely heavy. AMD should fall back to its 20-day moving average at $470, for example. That is a high-risk trade, though. If President Trump announces new talks with Iran, AMD could instantly be back at new highs.
 
Headline risk cuts both ways.
 
TSLA is getting hit by higher rates. The economics of selling high-ticket items like cars becomes more difficult as financing costs rise. We need shares to close above $414 today. That level is important.
 
META continues to frustrate. Every time it looks like bulls are about to break through resistance, they fail. There is support at $618, and while we are confident that level will hold, we have a time problem with our calls. Options traders don't get paid for being right eventually.
 
Close the position today at 3:45 PM ET if shares are trading at $640 or less.
 
HOOD actually looks good. We want to give this until Monday before taking any action. The chart is building a small bullish flag above rising 20-day and 50-day moving averages. That is typically a constructive pattern.
 
We are going to retry buying MRNA into this pullback. Something is happening in healthcare and we want exposure.
 
