Happy Tuesday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy TSLA, Buy ENT, & Sell Remaining Half of META

 

Stocks are little changed this morning as traders weigh a new share offering from GOOGL and much better-than-expected earnings from HPE.
 
The GOOGL news is particularly interesting and helps explain some of yesterday's weakness in META.
 
Google is raising $80 billion through a secondary offering to help fund its massive AI data center buildout. Financially, it is a smart move.
 
Bears will argue it is evidence the company's AI strategy is failing. Bears continue to miss the bigger picture. They have been wrong about AI, and we believe they remain wrong today.
 
Separately, President Trump is easing tariffs on agricultural and industrial equipment. The move will affect products ranging from combines and harvesters to bulldozers and forklifts.
 
CAT is beginning to look poised for a run at new highs. Our preferred way to play the theme is ETN. We have a target of $435 on the stock and are adding a new recommendation today.
 
We were disappointed with META's price action on Monday. If shares cannot reclaim $640 by Friday, we plan to close the position.
 
In the meantime, we are establishing a two-tier exit strategy for the remaining calls fot META. We previously placed an order to sell one-half of the position at $7.00. We are now adding an order to sell the remaining half at $5.00. This gives us an opportunity to reduce exposure on a rebound while ensuring we do not let the position linger if momentum fails to return.
 
The same applies to HOOD. If shares cannot move back above $95 by Friday, we intend to close the position.
 
TSLA found strong support at $413, right at its 200-day moving average. Buyers stepped in where they needed to. As a result, we are adding back the second half of the July 17th $530 calls that we previously sold.
 
