Happy Friday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Buy P July 17th $90 calls at $6.50 or less

 

It is Friday and the S&P 500 is headed toward its eighth consecutive winning week, a feat achieved only twice since 2017.
 
Bears are freaking out because consumer sentiment is in freefall, interest rates are rising, and food prices are surging. Wall Street seems completely divorced from Main Street.
 
Unfortunately for bears, one is a forward-looking price mechanism. The other is backward-looking.
 
The rally is frustrating because smaller, speculative names are rising fastest. This is normal. Low-quality stocks rally in this environment because bears are getting squeezed. It is still frustrating because our better ideas, TSLA and META, are stuck in the rotation.
 
We are adding one new call position for P. We believe shares can reach $100 following a successful test of the breakout level at $75.
 
New Order:
 
➤ Buy P July 17th $90 calls at $6.50 or less, day order only.

 

