Happy Tuesday,
 
TLDR: No New Trades

 

The S&P 500 is trading lower as traders react to rising interest rates. The 10-year Treasury yield is now 4.7%.
 
That is a big problem.
 
Higher yields impact consumer financing. Consumer discretionary shares are getting crushed.
 
The higher yields are all about energy prices and the war with Iran. Fixed income traders are sending a clear message to President Trump: end the blockade of the Strait of Hormuz. Now.
 
If the president refuses to listen, rates will move higher, and the Trump Recession will follow quickly.
 
Professionals are rotating out of chip stocks and into software. This migration was inevitable. The SaaS Apocalypse narrative was always a myth. AI cannot operate without the baseline truth provided by enterprise software companies like NOW, MSFT, ORCL, and CRM.
 
TSLA opened below the $407 support level on rising interest rates. Bulls need to regroup. There is further support at $395 on the weekly chart.
 
META is hanging around. We are confident there will be a rally beyond the resistance point at $621 in the near term.
 
We closed RXRX on stop Monday for a loss of 43%. umph...
 
Nothing new today.

 

