Happy Friday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Sell USO & RTX at Market 

 

President Trump is threatening Iran again with annihilation and oil prices are screaming higher.
 
The S&P 500 is falling back, but that is not the real worry. Bond yields are soaring. The 10-year Treasury is now well above 4.5%.
 
Ten-year Treasury yields impact everything from car loans to credit card interest rates. The increase is bond traders saying enough. Bond traders can kill the economy and the stock market.
 
The good news is that President Trump seems to care about the latter. Expect the war rhetoric to be corrected later today or early next week.
 
Not so curiously, software stocks are moving up. Portfolio manager Bill Ackman took a big position in MSFT last quarter, according to a 13F filing.
 
Other software names are catching a bid. See NOW, CRM. While we like these stocks longer term, we still need to see them rally on bad news.
 
We are looking for a place to enter TSLA from the long side. The interest rate rise is worrisome. We can wait until next week.
 
We added META calls on Thursday. A close today above $622 would be a major breakout. We like this one a lot, especially as hedge fund 13F reports start rolling out next week.
 
RTX and USO have been bad trades. We foolishly let them become lottery tickets, holding for a miracle turnaround once they bombed. The lottery window ends today.
 
