We need this to reverse.
 
One day soon, stocks will rally despite a new upgrade from Anthropic or a lousy earnings report from some important software company.
 
That will be the bottom.
 
WMT is bouncing hard as traders sell tech. This is how it is supposed to work. Money rotates out of tech and into safe stocks like staples. We closed our May series calls at $6.90 for a cool 40.82% gain. 
 
APLD is zooming higher. Shares traded to $35. This stock should finally make a run at $40.
 
We have IONQ back on our radar. First target is $46.50. That trade might be a bit skinny.
 
PEP is almost noteworthy. Shares should reach $165, although we already have WMT.
 
Our favorite long is XEL. Shares traded as low as $77.24 and are now $81.76. First target is $86. We are trying some calls with a tight target.
