Happy Wednesday,
 
TLDR: No New Trades

 

The S&P 500 opened firmer and quickly found sellers.
 
We are not surprised.
 
Since 2015, breakouts to new highs have found sellers, not buyers. That said, it is curious that bears cannot break the leaders.
 
We put industrials like CAT in that category. We mentioned earlier in the week that CAT, DE, and ETN look tired. That is not terrible. CAT made a new high on April 13th above $800. The stock has support at $745, currently $756.
 
META tagged its 200-day moving average at about $680 but has yet to find real sellers. AVGO is also much firmer than we expected.
 
Perhaps it is headed for a test of the old high near $410.
 
Software stocks gapped higher in short-covering and found sellers.
 
These names are severely oversold but remain in downtrends. We still believe software will surge into the NOW earnings report next week.
 
This looks and feels like a consolidation day for the S&P 500. The onus is on bears to step up and push the index back below 7,000.
 
