Happy Monday,
 
TLDR: No New Trades

 

The S&P 500 is actually up after starting the session sharply lower on more saber-rattling in the Middle East. President Trump says he is going to blockade the Strait of Hormuz because Iran wants to charge tolls for safe passage.
 
We do not get into politics because it is not helpful for trading. That said, this is now about reparations for the destruction of Iran. The money will come from somewhere. That is how the market sees this conflict. The fighting is no longer the story.
 
Software stocks are snapping back violently, as predicted. The carnage in these names was beyond ridiculous. Investors are far overestimating the short-term impact of Anthropic's Claude. Sadly, these patterns are tough trades because they are newsy.
 
SHOP, SPOT, and ORCL are building constructive patterns.
 
We added a new call position late Friday for WMT. Shares are holding the $125.50 level.
 
RTX is rebounding modestly. This idea is not about the war with Iran. It is about new military budgets as resources are being rapidly depleted. We see RTX making a new high.
 
We are in the kind of stock market that befuddles bears. They cannot understand why negative news is no longer driving prices lower.
 
When stocks stop going down on bad news, sentiment has shifted.

 

