Happy Wednesday,
 
TLDR: Buy RTX Calls

 

The S&P 500 is ripping higher on news of a ceasefire with Iran. Bears are panicking. Pros aren’t comfortable either.
Institutional desks spent weeks dialing back global growth and dumping early-cycle stocks. Now they’re scrambling to reverse those trades as oil prices collapse.
This outcome was always the most logical. The U.S. can’t take out Iran’s oil infrastructure without sending crude higher, and Iran can’t shut the Strait of Hormuz without crippling its own economy.
The key question is follow-through. If this rally holds, the S&P is going to new highs — quickly. Pros are offsides, and we’re at the start of a new quarter. That’s fuel.
We missed GLW. No excuses. Shares are at a record high, up 7.4%. That one is on us.
On the tape:

CCJ opened above $116 and is holding. A move to $135 is in play. We’re looking at May calls.
USO is getting crushed as oil drops. Target is $98.50. Down 12% and still falling.
Semis are strong:

AVGO → $393 (gap fill)
LSCC → $108
ON → $72.20

We also like defense and data center suppliers here.

RTX → $212
BE → $170

We’re adding exposure to RTX.
Buy RTX May 15th $210 calls at $5.50, day order only.
Bottom line: Bears are trapped, oil is falling, and pros are scrambling. If the early gains stick, this turns into a chase higher fast.

 

