Happy Tuesday,
 
TLDR: No New Trade

 

It is Tuesday and stocks are soaring as the Wall Street Journal reports that President Trump is willing to end the war if the Strait of Hormuz does not open soon.
 
This is a strange story because it contradicts everything Trump has said publicly.
 
Still, this rally on Turnaround Tuesday was predictable.
 
Bears are covering short positions. This is not because they are worried. They still feel in complete control. They are covering because stocks came down too far, too fast.
 
These events play out repeatedly. Professional money managers panic. They start selling their winners.
 
Recall that on Monday, CAT, ETN, TER, and KLAC all suddenly collapsed. All of them are soaring today.
 
The stocks that should perform best for the rest of the session are the names that are deeply out of favor. NVDA could rally to $175. META could push to $580. GOOGL might reach $292.
 
These names are in bearish trends and bears have huge profits. This is a good place for them to book gains.
 
That is the problem with this tape. The most oversold stocks look the best, but gains could get wiped out at any time. The best bullish setups fell through critical support on Monday.
 
They are now broken, despite rallying this morning.
 
MTSI looks like it has to trade back to $197, but that feels too skinny for new puts.
 
The tape remains super choppy, subject to war headlines. A short-term tradable bottom could be developing, but bulls must hold the early gains.
 
Still on the sidelines.

 

