TLDR: ➤ Sell INTC May 15 $45 calls at $6.60, GTC➤ Sell CCJ April 17 $130 calls at $6.00, GTC

 

The S&P 500 is ripping higher after President Trump said the U.S. and Iran are holding “productive” talks and that planned strikes on Iranian energy infrastructure are off the table.
 
No surprise here. Targeting energy assets would have sent oil to $140 and created real economic damage. Also not surprising: the President claiming progress on talks. That’s always the off-ramp.
 
This has always been the bear trap. The biggest risk to the downside case isn’t fundamentals—it’s the President declaring victory and moving on. That’s exactly what we’re seeing today.
 
