TLDR: ➤ Sell CCJ April 17th $130 calls at $7.90, GTC.

 

It is Friday the 13th. Unfortunately for traders, the rangebound trading continues.
 
Some of this is energy prices stuck near $100 per barrel. Another piece is anxiety ahead of the weekend as the war with Iran continues.
 
Selling is concentrated in materials. This is a bet that $100 oil will collapse an already fragile economy. US GDP was revised lower to just 0.7% last quarter.
 
The other side of this debate is what happens to the price of oil if the Iran war ends.
 
Bears should be more worried about that.
 
We are still looking for a successful test of the March low at 6,639 for the S&P 500. We do not know if that comes today or not at all.
 
We do know we do not want to be short.
 
Financials are deeply oversold. GS is sitting on its 200-day moving average at $786. We are also watching crypto, often a leading indicator. Bitcoin is up 5%. Ether is up 5.6%.
 
Our only new setups here are MU and NBIS, a European AI infrastructure company. We have upside targets at $450 and $130, respectively.
 
We cannot take new calls until we get a resolution on S&P support.
 
CCJ is falling as uranium prices spike after President Trump says the US is not currently focused on an operation to seize Iranian uranium.
 
It is difficult to trade news, but this weakness seems like an overreaction.
 
