The S&P 500 is getting slaughtered as bulls concede a test of the 200-day moving average. That level is 6,590 and rising. The narrative is stagflation. Expect buyers to return on the test of the 200-day.
 
Stagflation is the idea of 1970s-style slow growth and out-of-control inflation. This is mostly a fabrication. Slow growth leads to demand destruction for high-cost commodities like oil. The math does not support the fear.
 
We really like the way data center plays are behaving. AVGO got a solid bid into the early decline. VRT and GEV have reversed early weakness. These businesses are doing extremely well with long runways of growth.
 
