Happy Friday,
 
➤ Buy C March 20th $120 calls at $5.40 or less. Day order only.

 

Stop me if you’ve heard this before. Traders refuse to buy breakouts, but they can’t resist stepping into pullbacks.
 
The buy-the-dip trade lives on as the S&P races back to 6,885, its 50-day moving average.
 
Keep in mind, this is a test of the underside of that marker. That is not normally bullish. In fact, rallies back to the 50-day often serve as a call to action for bears. We’ll see if they step up heading into the weekend.
 
The constructive news for bulls is leadership. Financials are back in charge. We love the way Bank of New York Mellon (BK) and Citigroup (C) are behaving. Unfortunately, we closed C during Thursday’s market air pocket. That one stings.
 
AMZN is getting a haircut after announcing capital expenditures will reach $200 billion in 2026. Aggregate 2026 capex for AMZN, GOOGL, META, MSFT, and TSLA now totals roughly $670 billion, up about 70% year-over-year. This is the real story behind the so-called AI “bubble.” See NVDA.
 
We are going back to C on an inevitable afternoon pullback. The key level is $119.
 
