Happy Monday,
 
TLDR: ➤ Sell C at $11.70 or greater, GTC

 

We’re starting the new month on firmer footing as bulls rotate back into big-capitalization tech. That’s not the story you’ll hear in the financial media, which is focused almost entirely on short-term weakness in NVDA and MSFT.
Look beneath the surface and a different picture emerges. AAPL, AMZN, and AMD are all catching strong bids. These stocks have been laggards. Money is rotating into names that have been out of favor.
That is not bearish behavior.
It’s also notable that deeply unloved enterprise software stocks are seeing short covering. ServiceNow and Oracle fall squarely into that camp.
We don’t trade these patterns, but technically NOW has a clear path to the gap near $130, and ORCL could grind higher toward $181.
The bigger point is simple: bears are running out of time. The S&P 500 is now just 26 points from 7,000, and the window for a broad downside break is closing fast.
We’re plugging along after a solid January, sticking to our patterns and taking profits when the market offers them.
We added Citigroup on Friday. Shares should work toward $124, and we are placing a new sell target.
OKLO had a poor close on Friday. We need to see shares reclaim $81 early this week. We’re holding for now.
AA is trading just below $57.50. We expected a sharper break and a quicker move toward $52.40, the rising 50-day moving average.
Remember, base metals remain oversupplied.
New Order
➤ Sell C March 20th $115 calls at $11.70 or greater, GTC

 

