Happy Friday,
TLDR: ➤ Buy C - Day Order & Buy AA - GTC

 

Stocks are trading lower as investors digest President Trump’s pick to replace Federal Reserve Chairman Powell in May. Frankly, we’re surprised by the negative reaction. Kevin Warsh is an excellent choice.
Metals are taking the brunt of the selling. Gold and silver are down roughly 7% and 15%, respectively. The thinking is that Warsh, who has deep Fed experience, will be more disciplined and less tolerant of policies that risk reigniting inflation. That narrative is gaining traction quickly. We’ll see if it holds.
Meanwhile, memory stocks continue to defy gravity. SNDK is soaring after another blowout earnings report. The stock was trading near $250 in December and is now north of $600. When we flagged the breakout a month ago, even we didn’t imagine a move of this magnitude.
We are not interested in chasing parabolic winners like SNDK, nor are we eager to catch falling tech stocks. Where we are interested is financials—especially banks—given the Warsh news.
Citigroup is setting up nicely. We see a clear path to a new high near $124, and we’re adding calls.
On the flip side, metals stocks remain under pressure. AA is getting hit hard. A decisive close below $57.50 should open the door to a move toward $52, near the rising 50-day moving average. We are adjusting our target accordingly.
 
