Happy Wednesday,
TLDR: ➤ Buy AA & OKLO

 

The S&P opened higher on another batch of better-than-expected fourth-quarter tech earnings. The index briefly tested 7,000 before falling back.
That’s not surprising. There are several things to watch today.
First, 7,000 is major psychological resistance. Bears believe they can fight there, and they are all-in.
Expect the usual narratives to get louder: Japanese debt, the AI bubble, geopolitics; pick your poison.
Second, heavyweight tech earnings begin in earnest. META and TSLA report after the close today, with AAPL tomorrow. 
These are narrative events, not accounting exercises. Nobody really cares about the numbers. Stocks will be re-rated based on what Zuckerberg, Musk, and Cook say about demand, spending, and the future.
Third, the tape feels heavy. Semiconductors are growing like gangbusters, yet ASML reported a monster quarter and shares are now trading lower after an early pop.
That tells you investors are looking to take profits in big winners.
Fourth, the FOMC policy statement hits at 2:00 ET. The outcome is not in doubt; we know what the Fed will do and largely what Powell will say. Regardless volatility always spikes around these events.
The bottom line is we are reluctant to chase the long side today. We remain bullish over the intermediate term and expect upbeat commentary from tech executives, but this is not the environment to force trades.
We could not get PSTG at our entry level on Tuesday. Stand aside for now.
We also missed AA puts. The entry level was wrong. Let’s try again.
We really like OKLO. The setup looks very similar to where PSTG was three to four days ago. The first target is $114. We are adding calls.
