The S&P 500 is back above short-term resistance at 6,800 and bears are scrambling to cover short positions.
The so-called Santa Claus rally effectively starts next week, and traders don’t want to be caught leaning the wrong way.
To read more about the Santa Claus rally on click here. 
Bears should be especially worried about the breakout in Palantir (PLTR).
Shares are trading above $191.
That’s real trouble for the “AI bubble” narrative.
PLTR is already viewed as one of the most expensive stocks in the market.
If it pushes higher from here, the short covering won’t stay contained - it will ripple across the entire AI complex.
We continue to favor memory makers like SNDK.
Shares could rally toward $280 as AI demand filters down the stack.
We also note a fresh breakout in KLA Corp. (KLAC) within the semiconductor equipment group.
Shares could run to $1,300, versus roughly $1,255 today.
Our positions in ABBV and MO continue to act well.
Big pharma is an underappreciated AI beneficiary, and consumer staples like MO should increasingly become a source of funds for the Santa Claus rally as money rotates into higher-beta names.
We know we haven’t been especially active.
Trading ahead of the holidays is tricky, as moves can be fast and fleeting.
That said, a strong close for the S&P today would likely flip the switch on a year-end rally.
For now, we watch and stay ready.

 

