Happy Wednesday,
TLDR: No New Trades + Holiday Publication Schedule

 

The S&P opened stronger but continues to get pulled back toward 6,760, its 50-day moving average.
The pressure is coming almost entirely from big tech, specifically the stocks that have carried the market in 2025.
The reason is straightforward.
More than 80% of actively managed funds are underperforming the S&P this year, largely because of the dominance of NVDA, GOOGL, AAPL, MSFT, and META.
Those names account for the bulk of the index’s gains.
