Traders have convinced themselves Apple played the AI cycle perfectly.
They did not — but that doesn’t matter when the herd wants in.
Retail is perking up ahead of Black Friday.
Same script every year: Buy the rumor (sales will be awful), sell the fact (sales are merely fine).
We’re still watching LULU, but we need a close above $173.
Patience is allowed.
MAR hit our target.
There’s nothing left to prove here — take the win and move on.
RTX is grinding higher.
We’re not sending reports tomorrow or Friday, so let’s put the target in place.
A push toward $179 seems doable.
New Orders
➤ Sell MAR December 19th $290 calls at $15.00 or greater, good-until-cancelled
➤ Sell RTX December 19th $175 calls at $6.40 or greater, good-until-cancelled

 

